From 11405d8846cc7f55d1ae998f8899f70d916d57d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:15:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(completion-recovery): a Desktop-delivered result
 is not offered again at the next start

deleg_e757744d (laptop-1, 11-12): the start-up reconcile reopened failed admission ca1d8f79,
the gateway's recovery note met the chat's turn lease, and the Desktop poller delivered the row
instead. Its transcript row stamps display_metadata.delegation_id (no admission id) and its content
lacks the gateway's INTERNAL NOTIFICATION footer, so _noted never matched it: every later start
would reopen the same result until 8 attempts or the 48 h replay cap.

- A failed admission's delegation counts as delivered when the target session (or its physical
  target) has an async_delegation_complete row stamped with that delegation id; filtered per id,
  so a coalesced admission reopens only its undelivered ids.
- requeue_admitted_completion(recovered_admission_id=...) stores the admission a reconcile reopens
  the row for (new nullable async_delegations.recovered_admission_id, backfilled by the canonical
  schema reconcile) in the reopening transaction and skips a pair already marked: "delivered again,
  once" now holds for consumers that stamp nothing (the batch consumer).

Tests: tests/gateway/test_completion_admission_desktop_delivery.py (a/b/c), RED on 2cc7101849.
